Our existing API has this pattern already shipped everywhere (see routes/orders.js):

```javascript
// GET /api/orders?page=2&per_page=20
router.get('/api/orders', (req, res) => {
  res.json({
    orders: [{ order_id: 1042, customer_name: 'Jane Doe', total_amount: 49.99, created_at: '2026-08-01 10:00:00' }],
    total_pages: 8
  })
})
```

Notice it uses snake_case keys, offset/page pagination, and a bare `orders` array key (no `data` wrapper). Now add a new endpoint to list a single order's shipments: GET /api/orders/{id}/shipments. Follow our existing conventions.
